    // ============================================================================
    // The Forsaken Realms - custom difficulty knobs (round 822, util/CustomDifficulty.java).
    // A save can change ONLY what is listed here: a value with no knob is dropped on load, and one outside
    // min..max is clamped. Deleting this file turns custom difficulty off (every save plays its preset).
    //
    // Each knob:
    //   id        the save's key for it (letters, digits, '_' and '.'); never rename one a release has shipped
    //   label     the name in the panel           tooltip   the full explanation
    //   category  the panel's tab                 group     a sub-heading inside the tab
    //   scope     "anytime" (Settings can change it mid-run) or "newGame" (new game and New Game+ only)
    //   level     "basic" or "expert"
    //   mode      "set" (the value replaces) or "scale" (the value multiplies each target's own value)
    //   min, max, step   the range; a percent knob is still stored as its factor (1.2, not 120)
    //   format    round 823: "percent" shows the factor as a percent in the panel (1.2 as 120%); a scale knob shows x1.5
    //   target / targets what it changes:
    //     tuning.field         a field of settings.json (data/TuningData.java)
    //     tuning.field{D}      the field's Easy/Normal/Hard/Insane set - the value goes into every column
    //     tuning.field[*]      every entry of a per-difficulty array, the same way
    //     difficulty.field     a field of the save's difficulty (config.json "difficulties", data/DifficultyData.java)
    //     rule.field           round 825: one of the player's Settings switches (data/SettingData.java), kept per save;
    //                          a new game starts with the profile's, and Settings changes the running save's;
    //                          never counted as "Custom" (the label means difficulty values changed) - logged as rules
    //     config.field         round 825: a plane flag of config.json (data/ConfigData.java), per save
    //
    // Plane flags kept hidden (round 825): ringGiftStart (off would hand the kit over at the start AND keep the Ring
    // Cities' gift talks), and the flags the game is built on - territoryControl, townReconstruction, colorReputation,
    // editionProgression, contentFilterTables, weightedSpawnTiers, functioningNeutralTowns, dungeonRotation,
    // tfrAchievements, cleanFont. showEnemyTierInName is a display preference, left to the plane.
    //
    // Never listed here, on purpose (they are not difficulty, and a bad value reads as a bug):
    //   speedUpMultiplier         the speed-up key's factor - the agent's 50x duels depend on it
    //   enemySpriteFrameCap       a rendering cap
    //   wrathDirectTiles, wrathReplanTiles, wrathReplanSeconds, wrathStuckSeconds, wrathWaitTiles
    //                             the Wrath hunter's pathfinding timings (a bad value strands or teleports it)
    //   spawnClockFollowsSpeedUp  the spawn clock's link to the speed-up key (a debugging switch)
    // Round 828 (the reader audit): left out as well -
    //   enemyTierScale*           each rank's size on the map (display; 0 draws an invisible enemy that still collides)
    //   legendLifetimeFactor      only legends on the old travel-time clock read it since round 350
    //   dungeonSourceShare        an on/off switch: 0 empties the world (the land's own roll stays held back)
    //   dungeonSourceRadiusTiles, dungeonSourceReachTiles, dungeonSourceMaxPerRoll, sameEnemyNearbyRadius,
    //   mapEnemyDefaultThreatRange, mapEnemyDefaultPursueRange   spawn and chase geometry
    //   spawnMinTiles, spawnMaxTiles   a min/max pair the panel cannot keep in order
    //   torchPulse*               the torch's light pulse (display)
    //   winStreakStartCards, archmageStartCards   card lists (content, not a number)
    //   goldLoss (difficulty)     read only when a difficulty sets neither defeatGoldLoss value - never in TFR
    //   spawnRank (difficulty)    the hand-placed object filter in places; only 0-3 mean anything
    //   startItems (difficulty)   an item list
    // ============================================================================
    // Round 823: the panel's tabs, in this order (a knob's category not listed here comes after them).
    "categories": ["Enemies & Duels", "Notoriety", "Economy", "Loot & Rewards", "Research & Sets", "Towns & Territory",
                   "Time & Pacing", "Rules"],
